
Once the dependencies have been installed in the Linux VM instance we can proceed to install the required Node (Design, Automation or API).

See Dependencies installation page to install the required dependencies

Disk space

Make sure that there is enough space in the installation data Folder. If necessary is possible to mount a data folder into an existing Disk following this documentation https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/linux/attach-disk-portal



To install the required node, follow the next bash scripts:

User

The following scripts cannot be run by super-user. Ideally the installation should be performed by a user created specifically for this purpose.



Design Node
$ ls -l
-rw-rw-r-- 1 dataiku dataiku 159284660 Feb  4 15:20 dataiku-dss-VERSION
-r-------- 1 dataiku dataiku       786 Jan 31 07:42 license.json
 
$ dataiku-dss-VERSION/installer.sh -d dss_data -l license.json -p 10000
-d → directory where the Design Node will be installed

-l → path to the .json license file

-p → port that the node will use

Automation Node
